[], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 22827, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Wot2y9Z5aQwQnydof3kQAd", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 27204, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-api back to v5.0.0 and opened a SEV2 incident, and the service is healthy again.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called \"payments,\" so I looked for similar names. payments-api was the one in trouble: v5.1.0, this morning's deploy, was unhealthy in us-east, us-west and eu-west with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** The release history has only two versions. v5.0.0 was healthy in production and v5.1.0 was degraded. I rolled back to v5.0.0 in all three regions. This didn't need change-manager approval because v5.0.0 has been healthy in production before.\n- **Check afterwards:** All regions are running v5.0.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, \"payments-api elevated errors after v5.1.0 deploy,\" and on-call has been paged.\n\nI only checked three service names: payments, payments-api and payments-service. If any other payments service had a deploy this morning, tell me its name and I'll check it too.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01CqozFogda9QJKA1sZcrz5v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019HX7cCL2sec7L2Bq6aiaNL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_018zANVwbxgaFThCqN9hVmt2", "c